# LLM Integration Standards (Rust)

> Apply these standards when working with LLM services in the Rust backend.

## Service Architecture

LLM services use Rust traits for abstraction:

```rust
use async_trait::async_trait;
use crate::models::{AppError, TextGenerationResponse};

/// Trait for LLM text generation services.
#[async_trait]
pub trait LlmService: Send + Sync {
    async fn generate_text(
        &self,
        prompt: &str,
        model: &str,
        max_tokens: u32,
        temperature: f32,
    ) -> Result<TextGenerationResponse, AppError>;
}
```

## Supported Providers

### OpenAI
```rust
pub struct OpenAiService {
    client: Client,
    api_key: String,
}

impl OpenAiService {
    pub fn new(api_key: String) -> Result<Self, AppError> {
        let client = Client::builder()
            .build()
            .map_err(|e| AppError::Configuration(e.to_string()))?;
        Ok(Self { client, api_key })
    }
}

#[async_trait]
impl LlmService for OpenAiService {
    async fn generate_text(
        &self,
        prompt: &str,
        model: &str,
        max_tokens: u32,
        temperature: f32,
    ) -> Result<TextGenerationResponse, AppError> {
        let response = self.client
            .post("https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions")
            .header("Authorization", format!("Bearer {}", self.api_key))
            .json(&request)
            .send()
            .await
            .map_err(|e| AppError::ExternalService(e.to_string()))?;
        
        // Parse and return response
    }
}
```

### Anthropic
```rust
pub struct AnthropicService {
    client: Client,
    api_key: String,
}

#[async_trait]
impl LlmService for AnthropicService {
    async fn generate_text(
        &self,
        prompt: &str,
        model: &str,
        max_tokens: u32,
        temperature: f32,
    ) -> Result<TextGenerationResponse, AppError> {
        let response = self.client
            .post("https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages")
            .header("x-api-key", &self.api_key)
            .header("anthropic-version", "2023-06-01")
            .json(&request)
            .send()
            .await
            .map_err(|e| AppError::ExternalService(e.to_string()))?;
        
        // Parse and return response
    }
}
```

## Factory Pattern

Use a factory to create the appropriate service:

```rust
pub struct LlmServiceFactory;

impl LlmServiceFactory {
    pub fn get_service(provider: LlmProvider) -> Result<Box<dyn LlmService>, AppError> {
        match provider {
            LlmProvider::OpenAI => {
                let api_key = SETTINGS.llm.openai_api_key
                    .clone()
                    .filter(|k| !k.is_empty())
                    .ok_or_else(|| AppError::Configuration(
                        "OpenAI API key not configured".to_string()
                    ))?;
                Ok(Box::new(OpenAiService::new(api_key)?))
            }
            LlmProvider::Anthropic => {
                let api_key = SETTINGS.llm.anthropic_api_key
                    .clone()
                    .filter(|k| !k.is_empty())
                    .ok_or_else(|| AppError::Configuration(
                        "Anthropic API key not configured".to_string()
                    ))?;
                Ok(Box::new(AnthropicService::new(api_key)?))
            }
        }
    }
}
```

## Request/Response Models

```rust
use serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};
use validator::Validate;

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize, Default)]
#[serde(rename_all = "lowercase")]
pub enum LlmProvider {
    #[default]
    OpenAI,
    Anthropic,
}

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Deserialize, Validate)]
pub struct TextGenerationRequest {
    #[validate(length(min = 1))]
    pub prompt: String,
    
    #[serde(default = "default_model")]
    pub model: String,
    
    #[serde(default = "default_max_tokens")]
    #[validate(range(min = 1, max = 4000))]
    pub max_tokens: u32,
    
    #[serde(default = "default_temperature")]
    #[validate(range(min = 0.0, max = 2.0))]
    pub temperature: f32,
    
    #[serde(default)]
    pub provider: LlmProvider,
}

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize)]
pub struct TextGenerationResponse {
    pub text: String,
    pub model: String,
    pub usage: LlmUsage,
}

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize)]
pub struct LlmUsage {
    pub prompt_tokens: u32,
    pub completion_tokens: Option<u32>,
    pub total_tokens: u32,
}
```

## Endpoint Implementation

```rust
#[axum::debug_handler]
async fn generate_text(
    headers: HeaderMap,
    Json(request): Json<TextGenerationRequest>,
) -> Result<Json<TextGenerationResponse>, AppError> {
    // Authenticate
    let user = authenticate(&headers).await?;
    
    // Validate
    use validator::Validate;
    request.validate().map_err(AppError::from)?;
    
    tracing::info!(
        user_id = %user.id,
        provider = %request.provider,
        model = %request.model,
        "Text generation requested"
    );
    
    // Get service and generate
    let service = LlmServiceFactory::get_service(request.provider)?;
    let response = service
        .generate_text(
            &request.prompt,
            &request.model,
            request.max_tokens,
            request.temperature,
        )
        .await?;
    
    tracing::info!(
        user_id = %user.id,
        tokens = response.usage.total_tokens,
        "Text generation completed"
    );
    
    Ok(Json(response))
}
```

## Error Handling

Always handle API errors explicitly:

```rust
async fn call_openai(&self, request: &Request) -> Result<Response, AppError> {
    let response = self.client
        .post(url)
        .json(request)
        .send()
        .await
        .map_err(|e| AppError::ExternalService(format!("Request failed: {e}")))?;
    
    if !response.status().is_success() {
        let status = response.status();
        let error = response.text().await.unwrap_or_default();
        return Err(AppError::ExternalService(format!(
            "API error (status {status}): {error}"
        )));
    }
    
    response
        .json()
        .await
        .map_err(|e| AppError::ExternalService(format!("Parse error: {e}")))
}
```

## Best Practices

1. **Validate inputs** before calling LLM APIs
2. **Log all requests** with user context
3. **Handle rate limits** gracefully
4. **Use appropriate models** for the task
5. **Set reasonable defaults** for parameters
6. **Never expose API keys** in responses
